# TestCopilotPermissionPathGrants stages its target directory HERE, beside the
# package, because it has to be outside both of Copilot's default path grants:
# the cwd subtree and the system temp dir. Everything under a temp root is
# inside the grant the scenario exists to measure the boundary of, so the
# staging cannot live there.
#
# The test removes it via t.Cleanup, so this only matters for a run that was
# interrupted — which has already happened once during development, leaving a
# dirty tree. Narrow on purpose: it names the exact prefix the helper uses and
# nothing else, so a real stray file in this package still shows up in
# `git status` the way it should.
copilotfixture-outside-*/
